media/gpu/v4l2: a buffer without a frame is a decode error, not a wait

With MMAP CAPTURE buffers the stateless backend wraps each free buffer
as a frame. When that fails (seen with a 10-bit VP9 stream announced as
profile 0: after the config change the buffer layout is one the frame
code cannot describe), CreateSecureSurface() returned nullptr, which the
decoder treats as kRanOutOfSurfaces and waits for a buffer to be freed.
The buffer is already free, so playback hung with no error and no
fallback. Report a backend error instead.

--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_decoder_backend_stateless.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_decoder_backend_stateless.cc
@@ -255,7 +255,13 @@
     DCHECK_EQ(output_queue_->GetMemoryType(), V4L2_MEMORY_MMAP);
     scoped_refptr<FrameResource> origin_frame = output_buf->GetFrameResource();
     if (!origin_frame) {
+      // A free buffer that cannot be described as a frame (e.g. a layout the
+      // format code does not handle) never becomes usable: returning nullptr
+      // here reads as "ran out of surfaces" and the decoder waits forever for
+      // a buffer that is already free. Fail the decode so the pipeline can
+      // fall back instead of hanging the page.
       LOG(ERROR) << "There is no available FrameResource from the V4L2 buffer.";
+      client_->OnBackendError();
       return nullptr;
     }
 
